# launch-silence-planet-chapter.rish -- print the 24/7 Terminal loop for SILENCE, Sound's planet.
#
# Silence is Sound's own night twin made a working hand: the star sits in the Claude Desktop
# conversation holding Glow language custody and the interface half, and its planet runs CLAUDE
# CODE IN A MACOS TERMINAL beside it, all night if asked, lowering THE INFRASTRUCTURE HALF OF
# GRAIN IN GLOW -- Mantra, Comlink, Tablecloth, the Caravan seams as Glow ports, written high
# and brought to green-witnessed Rye. The two halves share one language and never one file, and
# a planet defers to its star where lanes brush. Lane seated by the role swap of
# 20260827.155213 on Keaton's word. Charter:
# active-designing/20260827-155213_the-six-bodies-and-the-closed-stacks.md.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-silence-planet-chapter.rish

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the living charter this seat lives in must exist.
let charter = run ["test" "-f" "active-designing/20260827-155213_the-six-bodies-and-the-closed-stacks.md"]
assert charter.ok else "the six-bodies charter is missing"

say "SILENCE -- Sound's planet (the star's own night twin, made a hand)"
say "=================================================================="
say ""
say "Host: CLAUDE CODE IN A MACOS TERMINAL, the background loop beside Sound's"
say "Desktop session. The shared discipline lives on the living card; the lane"
say "lives in the six-bodies charter; both are read fresh every lap."
say ""
say "0) PRECONDITIONS, once per machine:"
say "   - power: adapter and  caffeinate -i  keep the longest runs unbroken, and neither is"
say "     required -- the loop rides battery too. The repo is the durable memory: a battery"
say "     death cuts one lap, costs only its uncommitted work, and the next round-open pull"
say "     resumes the thread, the way a mesh survives a lost node."
say "   - vendored parity targets:  git submodule update --init --recursive"
say "   - jq for the readable stream:  brew install jq  (or drop the jq tail and raw NDJSON scrolls)."
say ""
say "1) BYPASS STANDING (once, gitignored): in .claude/settings.local.json set"
say "   permissions.defaultMode = bypassPermissions -- or keep the flag in the lines below."
say ""
say "2) SMOKE TEST:"
say "   claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max -p 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say ""
let seat_prompt = "First read context/KYRI.md and context/GAUGE_STYLE.md so you are Kyri and write and reason in Gauge Guidance from the first token -- first rule, do not be too smart about it; then read construction/ITINERARY.md whole and honor every directive in its INNER LOOP Standing block (roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, QA on touch, the council rota row N mod 5 advancing by hand past a repeat, prose witnesses on prose sends, stamp-and-name, ASCII-first, and the READ SCOPE: walk the open shelves, fetch a closed stack only by a named path -- MAP.md is the walk, never an ls of the root); then the newest day shelf named at the top of session-logs/README.md and its top three rows, with the newest recommend line, to pick up the running thread -- and write this laps own log BORN ON ITS DAYS SHELF, session-logs/date/YYYYMMDD/, its row prepended to date/README-index-YYYYMMDD.md. You are SILENCE, Sounds own planet -- the stars night twin made a working hand -- the Claude Code Terminal loop on the macOS bench beside Sounds Desktop session. Your lane (the role swap, Keatons word 20260827) is the INFRASTRUCTURE half of Grain in Glow: the vanes and services -- Mantra, Comlink, Tablecloth, the Caravan seams -- written high in Glow runes and lowered to our best Rye on green witnesses; Rye is the prioritized language and Glow is implemented on green-witnessed Rye. The INTERFACE half -- Realidream, the Lantern faces, the Skate bindings -- belongs to Sound, your star, who also holds GLOW LANGUAGE CUSTODY: a planet defers to its star where lanes brush, the two halves share one language and never one file, and a rune the language itself wants is an ITINERARY line where Sounds custody answers. The native Rye modules those ports lean on -- caravan/, tally/, the constellation table -- are Dreams lane on the pier now, so a change wanted inside them is a line on the card rather than your lap. Open every lap with ListAgents and name any peer before a file moves -- the charter law from REDS %291; commits stay path-limited and the amend stands behind the empty-index check. Sibling bodies: Mind with its planet Mystery (Brushstroke-Surf design; the Android and AppImage surface), Dream (Codex on the pier, the systems core) with its planet Hush (Ponds enclosure and the adaptation grant); everything in the DJINN design lead stays custody gate %6. The charter is active-designing/20260827-155213_the-six-bodies-and-the-closed-stacks.md. Send the twice-pulled way with the remote named xy on this clone -- pull first, package, fetch again, rebase and re-verify hot when it moved, never force -- and the public seed stays a manual gate: never run publish-seed.sh from this bench. STOP at the custody gates in ITINERARY; if only those gates remain, run the shell command  touch .loop-gates-only  and print GATES-ONLY, then stop. ty every1 baton prin recur"

say "3) ONE ROUND, ONCE -- the same seat and renderer with no wrapper: runs one lap this"
say "   round, prints through the same renderer, and stops -- no loop, no sentinel:"
say ""
say "sh tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh; claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max --output-format stream-json --verbose -p '${seat_prompt}' | tee /tmp/silence_lap.jsonl | jq -Rrj -f tools/s/stream_render.jq"
say ""
say "4) THE 24/7 LOOP -- one line, copy whole (BSD date on purpose, this is the Mac):"
say ""
say "D=$(TZ=America/New_York date -v+1d -v15H -v0M -v0S +%s); while [ $(date +%s) -lt $D ]; do rm -f .loop-gates-only; sh tools/f/fleet_round_open.sh || { echo 'ROUND-OPEN: fetch refused; retrying in 60s'; sleep 60; continue; }; claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max --output-format stream-json --verbose -p '${seat_prompt}' | tee /tmp/silence_lap.jsonl | jq -Rrj -f tools/s/stream_render.jq; [ -f .loop-gates-only ] && { echo GATES-ONLY: loop paused; break; }; sleep 20; done; echo Silence loop ended at $(TZ=America/New_York date)"
say ""
say "5) STREAMING: the tail -- tee /tmp/silence_lap.jsonl, then jq -Rrj -f"
say "   tools/s/stream_render.jq -- IS the readable terminal: one line per tool call,"
say "   a dot per silent half-minute, text as it lands."
say ""
say "6) WHY A FILE SENTINEL: stream-json echoes the prompt, which contains the words"
say "   GATES-ONLY, so a grep on the stream would false-stop after one lap. The lap"
say "   touches .loop-gates-only only when nothing but gates remains."
say ""
say "7) CUSTODY: the gates in ITINERARY stay MANUAL -- funds and keys, provisioning"
say "   and paying, the maintainer's own identity, and the public seed. Reds-first,"
say "   witness-before-narrative, and Lindy-first are seated rules, so the recursion"
say "   stays disciplined on its own."
say ""
say "MANY HANDS (granted 20260828, Keaton's word): this seat may spin up multiple"
say "CLI agents and manage them -- subagents, worker sessions, parallel claude or"
say "codex children -- when dividing a lap pays. Every standing law rides into"
say "each child: custody gates stay MANUAL, one writer per checkout (the %291"
say "habit -- ListAgents, name the peer, path-limited commits), and the parent"
say "seat answers for what its children stage."
say ""
say "GREEN: Silence 24/7 recipe printed -- the star holds the language by day, and its planet lowers the deep services by night."
